{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Find the components that changed or went away, run code as changes happen, and pass messages"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between the parts of a program.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Detecting Changes and Removals","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ChangeTick","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/RemovedComponent"],"anchor":"Detecting-Changes-and-Removals"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A world gives you two ways to respond to what happens in it. You can look later: change","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"detection, removal records and events keep track of what happened, and the code that cares reads","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them when it next runs. Or you can respond at once: hooks and observers run a closure as part of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the change that fired them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Look later when the response belongs in a system that runs every step anyway, such as a health","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bar that redraws when the health changed. Respond at once when other data must never fall out of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"step with the world, such as a directory of entities by name.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Find-Components-That-Changed","text":"Find Components That Changed"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every component remembers the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/changeTick","type":"reference"},{"text":" at which it was added and the one at which it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last changed. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"changed(_:since:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"added(_:since:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" filters pass only the entities whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component is newer than a tick. Inside a system run by a schedule, leave out the tick:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"changed(Health.self)"},{"text":" then means “changed since this system last ran”. See “Find what changed”","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryingAWorld","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Those filters check every entity that holds the type. When few of many entities change between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"visits, ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/trackChanges(of:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" keeps a log of the type’s changes, so the filters cost time in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"proportion to what changed rather than to how many entities hold the type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Find-Components-That-Went-Away","text":"Find Components That Went Away"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A removed component leaves nothing behind to filter on, so the world records removals instead.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/removed(_:by:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" returns the entities that lost a component of a type since a reader last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"asked, whether by removal or by despawn. A reader is any type you choose, so different parts of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"program each keep their own place.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Recording starts at the first call to ","type":"text"},{"code":"removed(_:by:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or at ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/trackRemovals(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":";","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"removals before that aren’t reported. The record is kept as events are, so each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/updateEvents()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" drops the removals from before the previous one.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Run-Code-When-Components-Come-and-Go","text":"Run Code When Components Come and Go"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"hook"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is a closure the world runs when an entity gains, is given or loses a component of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/onAdd(_:perform:)-27g0l"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/onInsert(_:perform:)"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/onRemove(_:perform:)-2t2p"},{"text":". Given a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query"},{"text":" in place of a type, ","type":"text"},{"code":"onAdd","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"onRemove","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run when an entity starts or stops matching the query. A hook runs after the operation that fired","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it has finished, so it sees the whole spawn or insert.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Hooks don’t run for changes made in place, through the subscript or an update. Use change","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"detection for those.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example keeps a list of the fallen as they’re despawned, and reads the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"despawn from the removal record afterward:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct Fallen: Resource { var names: [String] = [] }","enum TallyReader {}","","var world = World()","world.resources.insert(Fallen())","_ = world.removed(Health.self, by: TallyReader.self)","world.onRemove(Name.self) { world, _, name in","    world.resources[Fallen.self].names.append(name.value)","}","","let knight = world.spawn(Name(value: \"knight\"), Health(current: 0))","world.despawn(knight)","","print(world.resources[Fallen.self].names)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"knight\"]\"","print(world.removed(Health.self, by: TallyReader.self) == [knight])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Trigger-Events-on-an-Entity","text":"Trigger Events on an Entity"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntityEvent"},{"type":"text","text":" tells one entity that something happened to it, such as a barrel being hit."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Register observers with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/observe(_:on:perform:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for one entity, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/observe(_:perform:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for every entity, and fire the event with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/trigger(_:on:)"},{"type":"text","text":". The observers run before "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trigger(_:on:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns. An event whose type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"propagates moves up the hierarchy ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ChildOf"},{"type":"text","text":") after each entity’s observers run, until it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaches the root or an observer stops it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Send-Messages-Between-Systems","text":"Send Messages Between Systems"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Event","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is a message one part of a program sends and other parts read later, such as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collision that a damage system and a sound system both respond to. Send one with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/send(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", and read it with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/readEvents(_:by:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". Each reader reads each event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Events wait in two buffers, and each ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/updateEvents()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" drops the older one, so an event can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be read for the rest of the step it was sent in and all of the next. Call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"updateEvents()"},{"text":" once a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"step, such as with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UpdateEvents"},{"text":" system at the start of a frame. Without it, events are never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dropped.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/reactingtochanges"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ReactingToChanges"},"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"title":"Reacting to Changes"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/trackRemovals(of:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/trackremovals(of:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"trackRemovals","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type)"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/trackRemovals(of:)","type":"topic","title":"trackRemovals(of:)","abstract":[{"text":"Starts recording every entity that loses a component of the given type.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/onRemove(_:perform:)-2t2p":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/onremove(_:perform:)-2t2p","title":"onRe